# Copy to .env.local for local dev or production builds.
# Point this at the backend ORIGIN (scheme + host [+ port]). It is used for API
# calls, WebSocket traces, downloads, and /outputs visualizer artifacts.
#
# Service code uses paths that INCLUDE the /api prefix (e.g. /api/auth/login,
# /api/agents/..., /api/chats). The FastAPI backend mounts everything under /api
# and does NOT strip it, so DO NOT add /api here — use the bare origin. (If you
# do include it, the backend de-duplicates the resulting /api/api and it still
# works, but the origin is the intended value.)
#
# VITE_BACKEND_URL is preferred. VITE_API_BASE is accepted as an alias.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://your-domain.example.com
# VITE_API_BASE=https://your-domain.example.com
